{
  "title": "Sakai Collaboration and Learning Environment (Sakai CLE) \u2014 EdTech/Learning Management System (1,216\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Sakai Collaboration and Learning Environment (Sakai CLE)\nDomain: EdTech/Learning Management System | Scale: large | Stars: 1,216\nProblem: Sakai is a comprehensive open-source learning management system and virtual learning environment that provides institutions with a freely available, feature-rich platform for education, teaching, research, and collaboration.\nTarget users: Educational institutions, Universities and colleges, K-12 schools, Research organizations, Learning administrators, Instructors, Students\nCore features: Course management and content delivery; Collaborative learning tools and workspaces; Assessment and grading system; User authentication and role-based access control; Communication tools (messaging, announcements); Research and project management capabilities; Integration with external learning tools and standards\nIntegrations: LTI (Learning Tools Interoperability), SAML authentication, Third-party educational platforms\nTech stack: HTML, JavaScript, Vue, SCSS, CSS + Java + Oracle (PL/SQL evident) + Apache Tomcat 9\nKey libraries: Maven (build tool), Vue.js (UI framework), XSLT (XML processing)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Enterprise-grade Java monolith designed for institutional deployment and stability over rapid iteration; multi-decade maturity supports diverse educational use cases\n- Modular plugin-based tool architecture allows institutions to customize and extend functionality without forking core codebase\n- Strong community governance model (Apereo Foundation) and long-term support strategy with multiple concurrent versions ensure sustainability and institutional confidence\n- Tomcat-based deployment requires careful configuration and institutional IT resources, reflecting traditional enterprise education software patterns",
